## Modifications

MPL-2.0 §3.1 requires recipients to be informed about the license and how to obtain the source,
and it is good practice to identify what changed. Files that carry upstream content, and the nature
of the change:

| File | Upstream origin | Change |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `src/constant.ts` | `src/constant.ts` | VK ID endpoints and default scope kept and documented; metadata description/form items rewritten; `clientSecret` form item replaced by `serviceToken`; timeout constant changed |
| `src/types.ts` | `src/types.ts` | Guards rewritten: callback no longer requires `redirectUri`; token-response fields made optional; config credential model corrected; redirect-URI/scope validation added; connector-session guard added |
| `src/index.ts` | `src/index.ts` | Callback pipeline rewritten: session-bound PKCE verifier, `state` and redirect URI; provider-error mapping; token/profile subject consistency check; secret-free error payloads; token response normalization |
| `src/pkce.ts` | upstream used `pkce-challenge` (bundled, undeclared) | replaced by a `node:crypto` S256 implementation |
| `src/http.ts` | new (upstream used `ky` inline) | platform `fetch` transport with a timeout/error taxonomy |
| `src/client.ts` | new (upstream logic was inline in `src/index.ts`) | VK ID API client and error mapping |
| `src/profile.ts` | new (upstream mapping was inline) | profile normalization, name/avatar/e-mail/phone policy |
| `tests/**` | new | written from scratch; the upstream tests were GitHub connector tests and could not run |
| `README.md`, `README.ru.md`, `docs/**` | new | rewritten from scratch; the upstream README described GitHub, not VK ID |
| `logo.png`, `logo-dark.png` | upstream logo files **not** reused | connector icon supplied for this project; it carries the VK wordmark and is used nominatively to identify the provider. VK and the VK logo are trademarks of their respective owners; no endorsement is implied |

No file from the upstream work was copied verbatim into this repository except the already-public
endpoint/scope constants and the resulting behaviour, both of which were re-derived from the VK ID
documentation. The provenance table is kept for honesty and to satisfy attribution expectations.

